* c7552_tran: c7552.net with every input a PULSE as gen_iscas.py's `tran` mode writes them
* (100 ps edges, period 2*(i%8+1) ns), and `.tran 10p 10n`: 1 000 print steps, the size of the
* ngspice/OpenVAF c7552 transient (~1 020 points). The staggered input edges make the step control
* accept more points than that (~2 500 by 2 h in a first, interrupted run). Derived from c7552.net because
* gen_iscas.py needs external/benchmarkExt/ for the cells, which c7552.net already inlines.
*
* ISCAS'85 c7552 at transistor level, PSP103, in the style of the c7552 deck in
* external/benchmarkExt/iscas85_benchmark_circuit/. Generated by gen_iscas.py from
* c7552.bench: 207 inputs, 108 outputs, 3512 gates.
* Cells are c7552's, verbatim; gates it lacks are composed from them (gen_iscas.py).
*
*   cargo run --release -p va-cli -- sim circuits/benchmark/iscas85/c7552.net \
*       --model benchmark/models/psp103/psp103.va --tran

.include ../../../benchmark/modelcards/psp103_nmos.mod
.include ../../../benchmark/modelcards/psp103_pmos.mod

Vdd vdd gnd DC 1.8
Vg1 g1_0 gnd PULSE(0 1.8 0p 100p 100p 0.9n 2n)
Vg5 g5_0 gnd PULSE(0 1.8 100p 100p 100p 1.9n 4n)
Vg9 g9_0 gnd PULSE(0 1.8 200p 100p 100p 2.9n 6n)
